DLL: Pop First
Implement the pop_first method that removes the first node from the list and returns it.

The method should perform the following tasks:

If the list is empty (i.e., the length is 0), return None.

Store a reference to the current head node in a temporary variable.

If the list has only one node (i.e., the length is 1), set both the head and tail of the list to None.

If the list has more than one node, perform the following steps:

Update the head of the list to be the next node of the current head.

Set the prev attribute of the new head node to None.

Set the next attribute of the removed node (stored in the temporary variable) to None.

Decrement the length attribute of the list by 1.

Return the removed node (stored in the temporary variable).

solution:

 def pop_first(self):
        if self.length == 0:
            return None
        temp = self.head
        if self.length == 1:
            self.head = None
            self.tail = None
        else:
            self.head = self.head.next
            self.head.prev = None
            temp.next = None
        self.length -= 1
        return temp
